{"agent_id":"agy-skeptic","role_summary":"Attack scope and cost, apply YAGNI ruthlessly, argue for the smallest schema that ships at a hackathon, and name what others are over-engineering.","recommendation":"Use two JSON files as the source of truth (one hand-curated per-crop evidence file, one gap registry extended to 8 crops) and a single flat SQLite table with one row per crop×axis, populated by a trivial loader script. Do not model provenance, applicability scope, growth stages, or calibration in the relational schema — store the full provenance blob as a JSON column for the rare audit query. Everything else is over-engineering for data that is 80% NULL.","why":["Across 8 crops × 8 sensors, only air_temperature has strong direct evidence; the rest are partial, mismatched, or empty — the real table is ~85% NULLs, so normalising it buys nothing","The gap registry + inline markers already ARE the provenance model; duplicating them into normalised SQL tables doubles maintenance for queries nobody has written yet","A hackathon team will spend more time on a 6-table schema migration than on the actual dashboard; one wide-ish table is queryable, debuggable, and shippable in a day","EAV / triple-store / event-sourced approaches solve extensibility problems this project will never have — 8 crops, 8 sensors, and a skeleton that hasn't changed across all docs"],"schema_sketch":"-- Source of truth: backend/docs/cropinfo/*.json (hand-curated)\n-- Loader: Python script reads JSON, INSERT OR REPLACE into SQLite\n\nCREATE TABLE crop_axis (\n  crop_id        TEXT NOT NULL,          -- 'basil', 'lettuce', ...\n  axis           TEXT NOT NULL,          -- 'air_temp', 'air_humidity', 'light', 'co2', 'pm', 'noise', 'soil_moisture', 'soil_temp'\n  score_policy   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'record_only',  -- 'scorable' | 'advisory' | 'record_only'\n  optimum_lo     REAL,                   -- NULL if no direct evidence\n  optimum_hi     REAL,                   -- NULL if no direct evidence\n  caution_lo     REAL,\n  caution_hi     REAL,\n  danger_lo      REAL,\n  danger_hi      REAL,\n  unit           TEXT,                   -- 'C', '%RH', 'lux', 'ppm', 'dB', '%VWC'\n  value_kind     TEXT,                   -- 'growth_optimum' | 'disease_risk' | 'experimental_condition' | 'injury_threshold'\n  measurement_basis TEXT,                -- 'field_capacity_ratio' | 'irrigation_water_ec' | 'nutrient_ec' | 'ppfd' | NULL\n  guidance_text  TEXT,                   -- Section 9 prose for advisory/record-only axes\n  evidence_json  TEXT,                   -- JSON blob: sources, cultivar, system, stage, gap_status\n  PRIMARY KEY (crop_id, axis)\n);\n\n-- Example rows:\n-- ('basil','air_temp','scorable',25,30,NULL,NULL,NULL,12,'C','growth_optimum',NULL,'보온하고...', '{\"sources\":[\"Walters 2019\"],\"gap_status\":null}')\n-- ('basil','air_humidity','advisory',NULL,NULL,NULL,85,NULL,NULL,'%RH','disease_risk',NULL,'환기하고...', '{\"sources\":[\"UConn Extension\"],\"value_kind\":\"disease_risk\",\"gap_status\":\"no_direct_evidence\"}')\n-- ('lettuce','soil_moisture','record_only',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'%VWC',NULL,'sensor_vwc_vs_field_capacity','균일 관수...', '{\"gap_status\":\"no_direct_evidence\"}')\n-- ('basil','noise','record_only',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dB',NULL,NULL,NULL, '{\"gap_status\":\"not_a_recognised_factor\"}')\n\n-- That's it. 8 crops × 8 axes = 64 rows. The whole DB is hand-auditable.\n-- Scoring layer later does: SELECT * FROM crop_axis WHERE crop_id=? AND score_policy='scorable' AND optimum_lo IS NOT NULL","scorable_axes":["air_temperature — only axis with direct literature optima across multiple crops","soil_temperature — germination-stage evidence exists for most crops, usable if stage-gated"],"unscorable_axes":["air_humidity — documented values are disease-risk thresholds, not growth optima; scoring them as optima is a category error","illuminance/lux — sensor unit mismatches PPFD/DLI evidence; no conversion without spectrum calibration","soil_moisture — measurement basis mismatch (field capacity vs pot sensor VWC) flagged measurement_not_transferable everywhere","CO2 — one basil interaction study only, no per-crop optima exist","particulate_matter — zero evidence in entire corpus","noise — not a horticultural factor; scoring it would be pseudoscience"],"assumptions":["The 10-section skeleton is stable enough that a hand-curated JSON intermediate can be produced in <1 day per crop","64 rows is small enough that a single developer can verify every cell against the markdown source","Provenance queries (who cited what, when) will not be needed before the hackathon demo; a JSON blob defers that cost without losing data","The scoring layer can tolerate a flat table because the number of scorable axes per crop is ≤2"],"risks":["A JSON evidence blob is not queryable by SQL; if the scoring layer needs to filter by cultivar×system, this schema forces application-level parsing","Hand-curation introduces human error with no automated reproducibility; a document revision could silently desync the DB","Collapsing all value kinds into one row per axis loses multi-valued data (basil has both an optimum AND an injury threshold for air_temp); the worked schema above would need a compound key or multiple rows, which pushes toward the EAV others will propose","If the project outlives the hackathon, the JSON blob becomes technical debt that a normalised provenance table would have prevented"],"cheap_validation":"Write a 30-line Python script that, for each of the 8 markdown files, counts the occurrences of '직접 근거 없음' per section 2-7 and prints a sparsity matrix (crop × axis). If >80% of cells are empty, the flat 64-row table is justified. If <60%, reconsider normalisation. This takes <30 minutes.","change_mind_if":"If the sparsity check shows that more than 3 sensor axes per crop have both optimum AND alarm values with direct evidence — meaning the table is more full than empty — then a normalised multi-row-per-axis schema becomes worth the build cost. Or if the product owner confirms that per-cultivar, per-system filtering must work in the MVP demo, then the evidence_json blob is insufficient and scope columns must be promoted to real SQL columns."}
